---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import Features from '~/components/widgets/Features.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <Hero>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Privacy <span class="text-accent dark:text-white">Policy</span>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      <span class="text-lg"> Last updated: August 2, 2026 </span>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Privacy Content -->
  <section class="px-4 py-16 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <div class="p-6 bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-900/20 rounded-lg border border-green-200 dark:border-green-800 mb-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-green-900 dark:text-green-100">Our Privacy Promise</h3>
        <p class="text-green-900 dark:text-green-100 mb-2">
          <strong>We don't collect, store, or transmit any of your personal data. Period.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-green-900 dark:text-green-100">
          123 ToDo is designed from the ground up to respect your privacy. Everything you do in the app stays on your
          device by default. We can't see your tasks, and we don't want to. The optional Google Drive Sync stores an
          AES-256 encrypted copy in <em>your own</em> Google Drive — only you hold the decryption key.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how 123 ToDo, operated by <strong>Unforgettable Management Ltd</strong> ("we," "us," or "our"), handles your information. Unlike most privacy
        policies that explain what data is collected, ours explains what we DON'T collect — and is transparent about
        the limited, user-controlled data that optionally flows through Google Drive Sync.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We DON'T Collect</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo does not collect, store, transmit, or process any of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Personal information</strong> - No names, emails, phone numbers, or addresses</li>
        <li><strong>Account data</strong> - No usernames, passwords, or login credentials (Google OAuth is handled directly by Google)</li>
        <li><strong>Task data</strong> - Your tasks, notes, and todos are never sent to our servers in any form</li>
        <li><strong>Usage analytics</strong> - No tracking of how you use the app</li>
        <li><strong>Device information</strong> - No device IDs, operating system info, or hardware details</li>
        <li><strong>Location data</strong> - No GPS coordinates or location tracking</li>
        <li><strong>Browser data</strong> - No cookies, fingerprinting, or tracking pixels</li>
        <li><strong>IP addresses</strong> - No logging of your network information</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How Your Data Is Stored</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo uses a layered, privacy-first storage approach:</p>

      <h3>Local Storage (Default — All Users)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your tasks are stored in your browser's localStorage and IndexedDB</li>
        <li>Data never leaves your device unless you explicitly enable Google Drive Sync</li>
        <li>We have zero access to your locally stored data</li>
        <li>Clearing browser data will delete your local tasks permanently</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Shadow Backups (Automatic — All Users)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>A secondary copy of your data is maintained automatically within your browser</li>
        <li>This exists entirely on your device and is not transmitted anywhere</li>
        <li>It provides a safety net against accidental data loss within the same browser</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Google Drive Sync (Optional — User-Initiated)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>If you choose to enable Google Drive Sync, your data is <strong>encrypted on your device</strong> using AES-256 encryption with a passphrase only you know, before being uploaded to your personal Google Drive</li>
        <li>We never receive, see, or store your unencrypted task data or your passphrase</li>
        <li>The encrypted file is stored in a dedicated folder in <em>your</em> Google Drive account — not ours</li>
        <li>This feature requires you to sign in with your Google account via OAuth 2.0 — a standard, secure authentication method managed entirely by Google</li>
        <li>You can revoke 123 ToDo's Google Drive access at any time via your Google Account security settings</li>
        <li>Data stored in your Google Drive is subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. No 123 ToDo Servers — What This Really Means</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo operates entirely client-side in your browser. We do not operate:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Application servers that process your task data</li>
        <li>Database servers that store your information</li>
        <li>Analytics servers that track your usage</li>
        <li>Cloud storage services for your tasks (Google Drive Sync uses <em>your</em> Google Drive, not ours)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The only server interaction with our infrastructure occurs when your browser initially loads the app's static
        files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript). After that, everything runs locally. Google Drive Sync communicates directly
        between your browser and your Google Drive — we are not an intermediary.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo's core app does not integrate with any third-party tracking or analytics services. Specifically, we do not use:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Analytics services (Google Analytics, Mixpanel, etc.)</li>
        <li>Advertising networks</li>
        <li>Social media tracking pixels</li>
        <li>Payment processors (the app is completely free)</li>
        <li>Email marketing services</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Drive (optional sync only):</strong> If you enable Google Drive Sync, your browser communicates
        with Google's APIs to store your encrypted data in your personal Google Drive. This is governed entirely by
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms of Service</a>.
        We only request the minimum OAuth permissions necessary to read and write a dedicated sync file in your Drive.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Progressive Web App (PWA) Functionality</h2>
      <p>
        When you install 123 ToDo as a PWA, the app uses service workers to enable offline functionality. Service
        workers cache the app's files locally on your device so it works without internet. This caching happens entirely
        on your device and does not transmit data to our servers.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Export/Import & Backup Features</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo provides multiple ways to manage and protect your data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Manual Export:</strong> Download your tasks as a JSON file saved directly to your device — no data transmitted to us</li>
        <li><strong>Manual Import:</strong> Restore from a previously exported file or import tasks from Todoist CSV — processed locally on your device</li>
        <li><strong>Google Drive Sync:</strong> Automatic encrypted backup and cross-device sync via your own Google Drive (opt-in)</li>
        <li><strong>Shadow Backup:</strong> Automatic local redundancy within your browser</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Data Security & Encryption</h2>
      <p>Your data security depends on the storage method you choose:</p>

      <h3>Local Storage</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Isolated per domain — only 123todo.com can access its own localStorage data</li>
        <li>Cannot be accessed by other websites</li>
        <li>Remains on your device unless you explicitly clear it</li>
        <li>Security is as strong as your device's own security (screen lock, passwords, biometrics)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Google Drive Sync</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Data is encrypted on-device using <strong>AES-256 zero-knowledge encryption</strong> before upload</li>
        <li>Only you — with your passphrase — can decrypt it. Not even Google can read it</li>
        <li>Your passphrase is never transmitted, stored, or recoverable by us</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        <strong>Security Note:</strong> If someone gains physical or remote access to your unlocked device and browser, they could
        potentially access your local localStorage data. Keep your device secure with passwords and biometrics.
        For enhanced security across devices, Google Drive Sync provides encrypted cloud storage that requires
        your passphrase to access.
      </p>

      <h2>9. No Cookies</h2>
      <p>123 ToDo does not use cookies of any kind:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>No session cookies</li>
        <li>No authentication cookies</li>
        <li>No tracking cookies</li>
        <li>No third-party cookies</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google OAuth authentication for Drive Sync uses Google's own secure session management — not cookies set by us.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Because we don't collect any personal data, 123 ToDo is safe for users of all ages, including children under 13. We
        comply with COPPA (Children's Online Privacy Protection Act) by virtue of not collecting any personal
        information from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>11. GDPR Compliance</h2>
      <p>For users in the European Union, 123 ToDo is fully GDPR-compliant because:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't process or control any personal data on our servers</li>
        <li>No consent is needed for the core app (nothing to consent to)</li>
        <li>Google Drive Sync is entirely opt-in and can be revoked at any time</li>
        <li>No data subject access requests are necessary (we have no data)</li>
        <li>No data portability issues (your data stays in your hands)</li>
        <li>No right to erasure concerns (you control deletion via browser settings and Google Drive)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>12. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</h2>
      <p>For California residents, 123 ToDo complies with CCPA because:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't sell personal information (we don't have any)</li>
        <li>We don't collect personal information for business purposes</li>
        <li>No opt-out mechanisms are needed (nothing to opt out of)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>13. Data Breaches</h2>
      <p>
        Because we don't collect or store user data on our servers, there is no centralized data that could be breached
        by us. Your local data security depends entirely on your device security. Your Google Drive Sync data is
        protected by AES-256 encryption, meaning that even if your Google Drive were compromised, your task data
        would be unreadable without your passphrase.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated
        "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.
      </p>
      <p>
        However, our core privacy principle will never change: <strong
          >We will never collect, store, or transmit your personal data to our own servers.</strong
        >
      </p>

      <h2>15. Transparency</h2>
      <p>
        123 ToDo is built with transparency in mind. You can inspect the source code to verify that we're not tracking
        or collecting data. We encourage technical users to review the code and hold us accountable.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Your Control Over Data</h2>
      <p>You have complete control over your 123 ToDo data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Export</strong> - Download your tasks as JSON anytime</li>
        <li><strong>Delete Local</strong> - Clear browser data to remove all local tasks</li>
        <li><strong>Google Drive Sync</strong> - Encrypted automatic backup and cross-device sync (opt-in)</li>
        <li><strong>Revoke Google Access</strong> - Remove 123 ToDo's Drive access via your Google Account settings at any time</li>
        <li><strong>Transfer</strong> - Move data between devices using export/import or Google Drive Sync</li>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> - View all your data directly in the app</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>17. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how 123 ToDo handles data, please visit our website at <a
          href="https://www.123todo.com"
          class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">www.123todo.com</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>18. Legal Basis</h2>
      <p>
        Because 123 ToDo does not collect or process personal data on our own servers, we do not require a legal basis
        for data processing under privacy regulations like GDPR. The optional Google Drive Sync uses your explicit
        consent (opt-in) as its legal basis for processing, which you may withdraw at any time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Privacy Features -->
  <Features
    id="privacy-features"
    tagline="Privacy by Design"
    title="How we protect your privacy"
    subtitle="Privacy isn't a feature — it's our foundation"
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Local-First Storage',
        description: 'All tasks stored in your browser by default. Nothing sent to our servers, ever.',
        icon: 'tabler:database',
      },
      {
        title: 'Zero-Knowledge Encryption',
        description: 'Google Drive Sync uses AES-256 encryption on your device. Not even we can read your data.',
        icon: 'tabler:lock',
      },
      {
        title: 'No Tracking',
        description: 'Zero analytics, zero cookies, zero fingerprinting. We have no idea how you use the app.',
        icon: 'tabler:eye-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'No Accounts Required',
        description: 'No email required, no passwords to remember, no personal information collected. Ever.',
        icon: 'tabler:user-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'Offline First',
        description: 'Works completely offline. No internet connection required for core functionality.',
        icon: 'tabler:wifi-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'Your Control',
        description: 'Export, sync, delete, or transfer your data anytime. You own it, you control it.',
        icon: 'tabler:shield-check',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- Final Note -->
  <section class="px-4 py-16 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="p-8 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800 text-center">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy Questions?</h3>
      <p class="text-lg mb-4">
        If you're wondering whether we collect something specific, the answer is almost certainly "no."
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg">
        Our core principle: <strong>Local storage by default. No tracking. Zero-knowledge encryption for optional sync.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
